    "title": "It Doesn't Take 21 Days To Build A Habit #shorts",
    "description": "Day 21 and it still feels hard? You're not failing. You're early.\n\nWhen researchers tracked people building a new daily habit, it took about 66 days on average before it felt automatic, and some people took much longer. The \"21 days\" idea isn't what the research found. The good news: missing a single day didn't meaningfully set people back.\n\nKeep showing up. Miss a day, start again the next.\n\nResearch: Lally et al. (2010), \"How Are Habits Formed\", European Journal of Social Psychology.\n\n#shorts #habits #discipline #psychology #motivation #animation #selfimprovement",
